## Context

After the figure rename (a61a3f2..d1fe235 on main), two code locations
still call Figure 2 "Pareto" in comments/docstrings:

- `src/aedist/palette.toml:94` — comment "Figure 2 (Pareto) to colour models by"
- `src/aedist/util.py:127` — docstring "Figure 2 (Pareto). Distinct from..."

These are non-functional but factually misleading after the split into
the cost × quality scatter. Also worth a second pass on the historical
reply notes in `slides/manuscript/synopsys-experiment1-replies.md` (the
"Pareto frontier placeholder" language is from when Figure 2 was a
placeholder; it now exists, and is not a Pareto frontier).

## Exit criteria

- [ ] palette.toml comment updated to reference cost × quality
- [ ] util.py docstring updated similarly
- [ ] reply notes in synopsys-experiment1-replies.md either updated to
      reflect current figure 2 reality, or marked clearly as historical
      review correspondence (keep as-is is also acceptable if framed)
- [ ] grep for "Pareto" / "pareto" in src/aedist/ and slides/manuscript/
      returns only deliberate uses (caption disclaimer, slide title that
      explicitly says "no Pareto front")
